  "note": "Triennial election of the twelve councillors (nomination day 7 May; polling day, had there been a contest, 21 May 1952). The three aldermen elected in 1949 held office for a further three years (Lurgan Mail, 2 May 1952). Twelve nominations, \"all official Unionists\", were received for the twelve seats; the first six named were retiring councillors. V. M. Harper and J. Ogle did not seek re-election."
